-- Large beside large, small beside small, and one column wholly inside the subnormals. big cancels to 0 before the trailing 1 arrives, so the left recurrence answers 1 where a right fold answers 0; small loses its 1e-320 head into a normal neighbour, so the left recurrence answers exactly 0 where a right fold answers 1e-320.
-- Below 1e-9 the --! out comparator is blind, so the small and grain claims are pinned as exact equality against a declared column rather than as a printed value.
--! registry ../registries/140-magnitude-extremes.reg

--! out 1
+/ Big

--! out 1e300 3e300 0 1
+\ Big

--! out 0 0 0 1
(+\ Big) == (+/ Big)

--! out 1 1 1 1
(+/ Small) == Zero

--! out 0 0 1 1
(+\ Small) == Zero

--! out 0 0 1 1
(+\ Small) == (+/ Small)

--! out 1 1 1 1
(+/ Grain) == Unit

--! out 0 0 1 1
(+\ Grain) == (+/ Grain)
